# Copy to .env on the central host before running `docker compose up`.
# The create-central.sh bootstrap script fills these in automatically; this
# file exists for documentation and for operators doing manual recoveries.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BuildBarn control-plane image tags. These are pinned PER COMPONENT — the
# upstream bb-deployments repo pins different tags for different images
# because bb-storage, bb-scheduler, bb-browser, bb-worker and bb-runner-
# installer are published from independent commits. Copy the tags from the
# currently-working barn-psmdb (or bump deliberately after a compatibility
# check) — don't just sync them all to the same string.
#
# Current defaults mirror barn-psmdb as of 2026-04-15:
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BB_STORAGE_TAG=20260326T151518Z-d0c6f26
BB_SCHEDULER_TAG=20260326T163248Z-e6ab874
BB_BROWSER_TAG=20260319T101727Z-1731858

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Envoy proxy (used as the REAPI v2 gateway for Bazel clients).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENVOY_IMAGE_TAG=v1.31-latest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private Hetzner network IP of this host (network 11374636 / psmdb.cd).
# Used to bind ports 8981 (Envoy/clients) and 8983 (worker gRPC) to the
# private interface ONLY — public interface never sees them.
# Discovered and written by create-central.sh via `hcloud server describe`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIVATE_IP=10.0.0.X

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scaler — autoscale daemon (Phase 2).
#
# HCLOUD_TOKEN: Hetzner Cloud API token with read+write on servers, networks,
# and SSH keys, scoped to the project that owns bb-psmdb-ondemand. Injected
# by create-central.sh; DO NOT commit a real token to git.
#
# SCALER_DRY_RUN: when true, the scaler logs "would spawn / would delete"
# decisions but makes NO Hetzner API mutations. Ship in this mode until the
# operator has eyeballed a full scale-up + scale-down cycle in the logs,
# THEN flip to false. Safer than accidentally spawning 33 cpx42s the first
# day.
#
# SPAWN_THROTTLE_PER_POOL: maximum new VMs the scaler will spawn for a
# single pool in one tick. Default 1 = serial cold-starts (one VM every
# poll_interval_seconds until desired fleet size is reached). Raise to e.g.
# 5 during a release matrix to warm up all workers within a single tick;
# lower only if you observe cold-start contention at the Hetzner API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
HCLOUD_TOKEN=replace-me-via-create-central
SCALER_DRY_RUN=true
SPAWN_THROTTLE_PER_POOL=1
